  "title": "Sounds, greetings and courtesy",
  "note": "Latin has no j or w; this course writes consonant u as v (vir) and consonant i as i (iam). In Cicero's day c and g were always hard and v sounded like w. Church Latin, which the game's Italian voice approximates, says c before e, i or ae like ch (caelum: CHEH-lum) and ae like e.",
  "src": { "t": "Allen and Greenough, Alphabet", "u": "https://dcc.dickinson.edu/grammar/latin/alphabet" },
